{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础：从涨落到指数律","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/large-deviations-theory/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"why-large-deviations","title":"为何需要大偏差理论","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/large-deviations-theory/foundations/why-large-deviations","wordCount":1885,"readingTime":8},{"seq":2,"slug":"rare-events","title":"稀有事件的指数尺度","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/large-deviations-theory/foundations/rare-events","wordCount":1657,"readingTime":7},{"seq":3,"slug":"ldp-definition","title":"大偏差原理 (LDP) 的严格定义","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/large-deviations-theory/foundations/ldp-definition","wordCount":1523,"readingTime":7}],"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"基础-从涨落到指数律\">基础：从涨落到指数律</h1><p>大偏差理论最反直觉的一点，是它研究的事件&quot;本不该发生&quot;。大数定律告诉我们样本均值几乎必然收敛到期望，那么讨论它偏离期望一个宏观距离，岂不是在讨论一个概率为零的极限？关键在于&quot;多快趋于零&quot;。本章要说清的，正是这个衰减速度本身携带着丰富信息，值得单独成为一门理论。</p>\n<p>三篇文档层层递进。<a href=\"why-large-deviations\">为何大偏差理论</a> 先回答动机问题：把大数定律、中心极限定理、大偏差原理摆成三层放大镜，说明每一层各自看清尺度上的什么，以及为什么工程与科学中&quot;罕见但致命&quot;的事件恰好落在第三层的视野里。<a href=\"rare-events\">稀有事件的指数尺度</a> 深入衰减速度的骨架：稀有事件概率为何是 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>I</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e^{-nI}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8413em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8413em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> 而非多项式衰减，速度 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span></span></span></span></span> 与尺度的含义，以及介于中心极限与大偏差之间的中等偏差地带。<a href=\"ldp-definition\">大偏差原理 (LDP)</a> 把前两篇的直觉锻造成严格定义：为什么要用上界配闭集、下界配开集这套看似别扭的表述，什么是好率函数与指数胎紧。</p>\n<p>本章是整个 hub 的地基，不涉及具体定理的证明工具（那是第二、三章的事），但它定义的每个概念——率函数、速度、LDP 的上下界——都会在后文被反复调用。读完本章，读者应能在遇到任何&quot;某个平均量大幅偏离典型值&quot;的问题时，立刻反应出&quot;这是一个大偏差问题，我该去找它的率函数&quot;。</p>\n"}